# Gazebo Sim fabrication GUI default camera — verified through cold boot

Date: 2026-10-01 (session M)
Operator goal: GUI starts by default with a close, correctly centred view of the
factory, and that view survives a full cold boot.

## Environment

- Server unit: `ao-sim-fabrication-gz.service` (active)
- GUI unit: `ao-sim-fabrication-gui-gz.service` (active)
- Installation: `ao-sim-fabrication`, `ROS_DOMAIN_ID=22`,
  `GZ_PARTITION=alwayson_fabrication_sim`
- World: `/ALWAYSON/GAZEBO/worlds/factory.world`
- GUI runs as **`gz-sim-gui-client`** — a client only.

## Persistent camera pose (authoritative location)

`/ALWAYSON/GAZEBO/.../gui-home/.gz/sim/10/gui.config` line 44, inside
`<plugin filename="MinimalScene" name="3D View">`:

    <camera_pose>9.0 6.5 2.6 0 0.22476 -2.5045</camera_pose>

Format is `x y z roll pitch yaw` (metres, radians). Framing target: the
`massing_fab.dae` mesh, measured 6.96 x 4.83 x 2.06 m, centred near
(3.48, 2.416, 1.029).

## Key finding — the world file is NOT the persistence mechanism

Because the GUI runs as `gz-sim-gui-client`, it never parses
`factory.world`. The `<gui>` block in that world (lines 69-73, 229) has no
effect on the startup camera. Only `gui.config` controls it.

The `<camera_pose>` inside a `<gui><plugin name="3D View">` block — which
coordination document L prescribes — cannot work here for that reason.
Document L is addressed in detail in "M. GAZEBO GUI default camera".

## Verification — full cold boot, no manual camera command

    systemctl --user restart ao-sim-fabrication-gz.service   # server down/up
    systemctl --user start  ao-sim-fabrication-gui-gz.service
    # no /gui/move_to/pose issued at any point

Result: the factory mesh renders in the close centred view. Capture
`/tmp/M_cold_full.png` (window 0x100001a, 687x330). Pose survives.

`gui.config` mtime unchanged across the restart (18:44:03) — the load did not
rewrite it, and the pose was read from it.

## Safe restart order

Stop the GUI before the server. Stopping the server first leaves the client
attached to a dead server and the viewport can freeze; a frozen viewport then
writes a stale pose back to `gui.config` on exit.

## Commands that do not work in this environment

- `gz topic -e -t /gui/camera/pose` and `gz service -s /gui/move_to/pose` —
  the in-container `gz` CLI has no working transport plugin. Helpers compiled
  against gz-transport are used instead:
  `/ALWAYSON/scripts/simulation/gztools/move_gui_camera.sh`
  `/ALWAYSON/scripts/simulation/gztools/read_gui_camera.sh`
- `xdotool`, `wmctrl`, `kdotool` are NOT installed on the host. Screenshot
  capture uses ImageMagick `import`; note `import -window root` fails, the
  window-id form `import -window 0x100001a png:/path.png` works.

## Open findings

1. GUI window opens at 687x330 at +582+1422 — small and pushed to the bottom of
   the screen. `gui.config` requests 1000x845 (lines 8-9) and the request is
   not honoured. No window-management tooling is installed to correct it, and
   installing packages needs operator approval. **Needs approval.**
2. `/gui/camera/pose` telemetry does not reliably match commanded positions and
   cannot currently be used to prove camera placement. Screenshot comparison is
   the only trustworthy proof. Not resolved.

