### OPEN BLOCKER — no camera data reaches Foxglove

Both hops run and the WebSocket serves, but ROS 2 domain 22 carries only
/parameter_events and /rosout. Foxglove will show an empty view.

Root cause (measured): **the world declares ZERO system plugins.**

    $ grep -c 'plugin filename=' /ALWAYSON/GAZEBO/worlds/factory.world
    0

The `user_camera` <sensor> at factory.world:269 is therefore inert: in Gazebo
Sim a sensor only publishes if SensorsSystem is loaded by the world. This is
independent of the bridge — no amount of bridge work fixes it. The GUI never
showed a problem because the GUI renders the scene directly and does not
consume sensor topics.

Fix requires adding to <world>:
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-sensors-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::Sensors"/>
plus the matching rendering plugin if the server needs to render headless.
NOT APPLIED — it is a world change to a live simulation and needs its own
operator approval and a server restart.

### Traps (each cost a failed build or a wrong conclusion)

1. Quadlet needs BOTH files. Creating the network with `podman network create`
   is not enough; without /ALWAYSON/quadlet/networks/ao-html-window.network the
   generator silently emits no .service and says
   "requested Quadlet unit ao-html-window.network was not found".
2. Regenerate with `/usr/libexec/podman/quadlet -user -v ~/.config/containers/systemd`.
   Without `-user` it reads /etc/containers/systemd and finds nothing.
3. Generated units cannot be `systemctl enable`d ("transient or generated").
   The generator already symlinked them into default.target.wants — just
   `systemctl --user start`.
4. A container unit deploys to ~/.config/containers/systemd/ as a COPY. Editing
   the /ALWAYSON/quadlet source changes nothing live.
5. foxglove_bridge ignores --port/-p/--ws-port/--websocket-port and binds 8765.
   Port is a ROS parameter: `--ros-args -p port:=8081`.
6. `set -u` in the entrypoint breaks ROS setup.bash
   (AMENT_TRACE_SETUP_FILES: unbound variable). Use `set -o pipefail` only.
7. Shell precedence: in "a && b & c" the whole "a && b" is backgrounded and c
   runs unsourced, losing LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Use a script file.
8. `gz` CLI in the server image is a stub: no topic/sub/service verbs, no
   gz-transport binaries (/usr/libexec/gz/ holds only sim10).
9. Foxglove WebSocket subprotocol is foxglove.sdk.v1.

### Correction to my own earlier claim

I previously reported the host had "no egress" and that Foxglove could not be
installed. That was wrong. The only command that would have tested it was
blocked by plan mode and I reported the tool block as if it were the finding.
The host has full egress and Foxglove installed cleanly. Lesson: do not state
a capability I did not measure.